# netsurf (MacSurf bridge): bytecode caches; big scripts keep no source
# Generated 2026-09-24
#
# Hardware run 16: every page built a realm parsing the same setup scripts
# (bundled test pages 1.3 s each), and claude.ai took 13 s to download its
# 19 MB of modules and 82 s to compile and run them, then ran out of
# memory (84 MB) on its dynamic imports.
# - Setup scripts (the bridge's and vita_polyfill.js) are compiled once and
#   read back as bytecode after (qjs_eval_cached): a realm takes 4.5 ms
#   instead of 16 on the desktop. "realm built" and "vita_polyfill" times
#   are logged.
# - Scripts and modules of 128 KB or more are compiled without keeping
#   each function's source text (patches/quickjs/02): claude.ai's heap
#   goes from ~99 to 76 MB (desktop).
# - Modules are kept compiled in ux0:data/VitaBrowser/jscache/
#   (MACSURF_JSCACHE_DIR) with their static imports. On a later visit a
#   module whose name carries a content hash ("index-DKU2AWSS.js") is
#   neither fetched nor parsed; others are fetched and their bytecode reused
#   when the text matches. Files carry the build stamp. "module compile"
#   logs how many came from the card. Past 96 MB the cache is cleared at
#   the session's first save (one claude.ai visit leaves ~40 MB).

